# C# parenthesis spacing

Space before `(` on calls, declarations, and primary constructors. Space after a cast.

```csharp
// BAD
public class SphMonsterData(SphGameObject sphGameObject)
public int HpPerLevel { get; set; } = (int)sphGameObject.MaxKarmaLevel;
monster.TakeDamage(amount);

// GOOD
public class SphMonsterData (SphGameObject sphGameObject)
public int HpPerLevel { get; set; } = (int) sphGameObject.MaxKarmaLevel;
monster.TakeDamage (amount);
```

Same spacing on methods, constructors, local functions, and `new`. Control-flow keywords stay as written (`if (`, `for (`, `while (`).
